      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.36,
          "end": 5.25,
          "en": "So now we wanna use our markdown files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.25,
          "end": 7.82,
          "en": "in the posts folder as a data source.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.82,
          "end": 9.88,
          "en": "For example, for the starting page here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.88,
          "end": 13.49,
          "en": "instead of using dummy posts, we wanna fetch our posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.49,
          "end": 15.97,
          "en": "from that post folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.97,
          "end": 19.22,
          "en": "for example with help of get started props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.22,
          "end": 20.83,
          "en": "Now, before we do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.83,
          "end": 24.36,
          "en": "I'll first of all create a new folder in the project though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.36,
          "end": 27.46,
          "en": "a lib folder or helpers folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.46,
          "end": 28.89,
          "en": "whatever you wanna call it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.89,
          "end": 32.827,
          "en": "And in there, I'll add posts-util.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.4,
          "end": 37.82,
          "en": "This simply is a file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.82,
          "end": 40.65,
          "en": "which will have extra utility functionality",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.65,
          "end": 42.99,
          "en": "for fetching my post data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.99,
          "end": 47.83,
          "en": "and for extracting metadata from those markdown files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.83,
          "end": 49.2,
          "en": "And speaking off that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.2,
          "end": 52.41,
          "en": "for this we need to install another extra package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.41,
          "end": 54.66,
          "en": "So quit your running development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.66,
          "end": 58.36,
          "en": "and install an extra package with npm install.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.36,
          "end": 62.1,
          "en": "And that would be the gray-matter package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.1,
          "end": 66.22,
          "en": "That's a package which allows us to read a markdown file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.22,
          "end": 71.22,
          "en": "and split it into metadata and the actual markdown content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.53,
          "end": 73.48,
          "en": "Once that's installed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.48,
          "end": 76.26,
          "en": "we can start the development server again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.26,
          "end": 79.33,
          "en": "And now in posts-util.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.33,
          "end": 83.58,
          "en": "I wanna add a couple of functions that fetch us all posts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.58,
          "end": 87.65299999999999,
          "en": "all featured posts and then also a single post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.13,
          "end": 92.25,
          "en": "Now let's maybe start with all posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.25,
          "end": 96.22,
          "en": "Let's add a getAllPosts function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.22,
          "end": 99.25,
          "en": "The idea here is that we take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.25,
          "end": 103.11,
          "en": "at this posts folder with the markdown files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.11,
          "end": 107.07,
          "en": "and simply check how many markdown files we have there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.07,
          "end": 110.28,
          "en": "and then go through all those markdown files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.28,
          "end": 113.18,
          "en": "to get the metadata for all those files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.18,
          "end": 116.63,
          "en": "Now for going through all those files here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.63,
          "end": 119.00999999999999,
          "en": "I will work with the file system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.00999999999999,
          "end": 123.09,
          "en": "and hence we should import fs from fs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.09,
          "end": 126.393,
          "en": "So import does fs node module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.624,
          "end": 129.42,
          "en": "And then here in getAllPosts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.42,
          "end": 132.61,
          "en": "I'll start by reading all the content from a directory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.61,
          "end": 137.13,
          "en": "with the fs module and the readdirSync method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.13,
          "end": 140.89,
          "en": "readdirSync will read all the contents synchronously.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.89,
          "end": 143.47,
          "en": "So in a blocking way, which is fine here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 143.47,
          "end": 145.96,
          "en": "because I wanna parse all posts anyways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.96,
          "end": 147.7,
          "en": "before I do anything else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 147.7,
          "end": 150.91,
          "en": "So I'll read the entire content off a directory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.91,
          "end": 152.81,
          "en": "in one go here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.81,
          "end": 154.53,
          "en": "Now we need to pass a path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 154.53,
          "end": 157.37,
          "en": "to the directory to readdirSync.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 157.37,
          "end": 158.47,
          "en": "And I'll create this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 158.47,
          "end": 163.02,
          "en": "as a separate constant outside of all those functions here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.02,
          "end": 165.01,
          "en": "I'll name it postsDirectory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 165.01,
          "end": 167.11,
          "en": "though of course, the name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 167.11,
          "end": 172,
          "en": "And then here, I'll import another thing from node JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 172,
          "end": 175.57999999999998,
          "en": "I'll import the path module here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.57999999999998,
          "end": 178.16,
          "en": "This allows me to construct an absolute path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.16,
          "end": 180.183,
          "en": "with the join method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.07,
          "end": 185.01,
          "en": "And here I join process.current working directory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 185.01,
          "end": 186.85,
          "en": "executed as a method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.85,
          "end": 190.38,
          "en": "which will point at the overall project folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 190.38,
          "end": 193.1,
          "en": "as you learned, not at this lib folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 193.1,
          "end": 195.96,
          "en": "but at the overall project folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 195.96,
          "end": 197.8,
          "en": "So that is then an absolute path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 197.8,
          "end": 200.64,
          "en": "to the overall project folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 200.64,
          "end": 202.84,
          "en": "and then I'll add posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 202.84,
          "end": 205.69,
          "en": "as an extra folder into which it should dive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 205.69,
          "end": 207.843,
          "en": "So this posts folder here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 209.41,
          "end": 213.26,
          "en": "That's then an absolute path to my posts directory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 213.26,
          "end": 215.78,
          "en": "and that's the directory I wanna read.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 215.78,
          "end": 218.363,
          "en": "So that's what I pass to readdirSync.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 219.76,
          "end": 224.76,
          "en": "Now this will return an array of strings, as you see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 225.1,
          "end": 228.39,
          "en": "In the end, it will be an array of file names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 228.39,
          "end": 230.293,
          "en": "So here I have my postFiles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 231.38,
          "end": 233.273,
          "en": "which are load with readdirSync.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 234.57999999999998,
          "end": 235.65,
          "en": "As a next step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 235.65,
          "end": 239.27,
          "en": "I now wanna go through all those post files and dive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 239.27,
          "end": 243.483,
          "en": "into them to extract metadata and markdown content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 244.49,
          "end": 246.92,
          "en": "I also wanna derive a slug",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 246.92,
          "end": 250.1,
          "en": "which can be put in the URL from the file name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 250.1,
          "end": 252.4,
          "en": "So basically I wanna use the file name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 252.4,
          "end": 255.67,
          "en": "without the extension, which still is part inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 255.67,
          "end": 257.173,
          "en": "of postFiles at the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 258.14,
          "end": 261.02,
          "en": "Now for this I'll add an extra helper function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 261.02,
          "end": 265.53,
          "en": "getPostData, sounds like a fitting name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 265.53,
          "end": 269.63,
          "en": "And here I expect to get the file name as an argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 269.63,
          "end": 273.86,
          "en": "Now in getPostData, we wanna read the content of a file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 273.86,
          "end": 276.2,
          "en": "We can again do that with the fs module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 276.2,
          "end": 280.02,
          "en": "And there, we have that readFileSync method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 280.02,
          "end": 282.27,
          "en": "for reading the content of a file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 282.27,
          "end": 285.88,
          "en": "Here, we need the fileName, but not just the fileName,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 285.88,
          "end": 289.75,
          "en": "we still need the full path to that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 289.75,
          "end": 293.76,
          "en": "So I'll construct my file path here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 293.76,
          "end": 297.11,
          "en": "by again using path.join",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 297.11,
          "end": 300.53,
          "en": "and I'll join this posts directory path with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 300.53,
          "end": 304.42,
          "en": "which we already have, with that file name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 304.42,
          "end": 307.36,
          "en": "So that constructs a full absolute path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 307.36,
          "end": 308.973,
          "en": "to that concrete file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 309.89,
          "end": 312.24,
          "en": "Now we can use this filePath",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 312.24,
          "end": 314.93,
          "en": "for reading the content of that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 314.93,
          "end": 317.11,
          "en": "We can always add a second argument here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 317.11,
          "end": 320.72,
          "en": "and make it clear that the file encoding is UTF-8",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 320.72,
          "end": 323.773,
          "en": "so that we support all those Unicode characters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 325.41,
          "end": 328.09,
          "en": "Then we got the file content here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 328.09,
          "end": 330.593,
          "en": "That's what readFileSync produces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 331.7,
          "end": 334.06,
          "en": "Now we're doing this for a single file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 334.06,
          "end": 336.8,
          "en": "So I'm not doing this in a loop or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 336.8,
          "end": 338.99,
          "en": "I'm just doing this for one file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 338.99,
          "end": 341.28,
          "en": "We're going to call getPostData",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 341.28,
          "end": 344.163,
          "en": "in a loop for all files later, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 345.02,
          "end": 347.88,
          "en": "But here we then have to content all the single file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 347.88,
          "end": 349.83,
          "en": "And now we know that in a single file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 349.83,
          "end": 353.33,
          "en": "we have this metadata and the actual content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 353.33,
          "end": 357.97,
          "en": "Now the overall content is what node JS extracted for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 357.97,
          "end": 358.83,
          "en": "To split it up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 358.83,
          "end": 362.13,
          "en": "we'll use this gray matter package which we installed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 362.13,
          "end": 367.13,
          "en": "So for this I'll import matter from gray-matter, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 368.51,
          "end": 370.63,
          "en": "And matter is simply a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 370.63,
          "end": 375.27,
          "en": "which we can call here to which we pass a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 375.27,
          "end": 378.21,
          "en": "And our file content is just a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 378.21,
          "end": 381.05,
          "en": "It's the content of a file as text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 381.05,
          "end": 384.01,
          "en": "So we pass the file content to matter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 384.01,
          "end": 388.84,
          "en": "and matter will then return an object with two properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 388.84,
          "end": 392.06,
          "en": "with a data property for the metadata.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 392.06,
          "end": 394.96,
          "en": "So a data property, which contains the metadata",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 394.96,
          "end": 399.13,
          "en": "as a JavaScript object and a content property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 399.13,
          "end": 401.03,
          "en": "which contains the actual content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 401.03,
          "end": 404.15,
          "en": "the markdown text as a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 404.15,
          "end": 406.34000000000003,
          "en": "So we can use object destructuring",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 406.34000000000003,
          "end": 409.67,
          "en": "to pull these two properties out of the returned object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 409.67,
          "end": 414.26,
          "en": "and store them in separate constants, data and content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 414.26,
          "end": 415.89,
          "en": "And these names are not up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 415.89,
          "end": 420.53,
          "en": "these are the properties in that object created by matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 420.53,
          "end": 422.143,
          "en": "So by this matter function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 423.43,
          "end": 424.94,
          "en": "Now that we got that,",
